Type: Package
Package: gcplyr
Title: Wrangle and Analyze Growth Curve Data
Version: 1.13.0
Date: 2026-10-14
Authors@R: person("Mike", "Blazanin", , "mikeblazanin@gmail.com",
               role = c("aut", "cre"), 
               comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-4630-6235"))
Description: Easy importing, wrangling, and model-free analysis of microbial
  growth curve data, as commonly output by plate readers. Tools for flexibly
  importing all the common data formats output by plate readers and reshaping
  them into 'tidy' formats for analyses. Tools for importing experimental
  designs from files or generating them in R and merging design information
  with density data, making it easy to analyze with 'gcplyr' and 'tidyverse'
  or 'dplyr' functions, and to plot with 'ggplot2'. Streamlines extracting
  parameters like growth rate/doubling time, maximum density (carrying capacity), 
  lag time, area under the curve, diauxic shifts, extinction, and more without 
  fitting an equation for growth to your data. Has several methods to deal with 
  noise in growth curve data. See methods at 
  <https://mikeblazanin.github.io/gcplyr/>.
